  "description": "DIJFUA crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C64 H98 N8 Ni4 O34 Tb4 2+,2(H1 O1 1-),5(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Tb01 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb02 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Ni1 (Ni) has 4 O neighbors; Ni2 (Ni) has 4 O neighbors; Tb3 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb4 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Ni3 (Ni) has 4 O neighbors; Ni4 (Ni) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 14 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.257-4.123 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 97.87-132.08°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Ni4Tb4(μ2-OH)2(μ3-OH)4(μ-OOCCH3)8(LH2)4]·(OH)2·5H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ2-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
